  "rendered": "In Table 2[1], the highest titer listed is for the sesquiterpene alcohol ((cid:0) )-α-bisabolol[2] (printed with a garbled minus sign for the stereodescriptor), reaching 102,300[3] in the units given in the column header (mg L^(cid:0) 1)[4], i.e. about102.3[5] g per litre. The producing strain is the engineered derivative HBQA7 → SMB19[6], obtained by Genome integration of the biosynthetic pathway and optimization of[7]precursor supply[8]. The conditions were a fed-batch[9] cultivation of 110[10] h, as reported in reference [22][11]. For comparison, the next-highest entries in the table are (2R,3R)-2,3-[12]butanediol[13] from strain MG1 → ΔslaC-bdhA[14] at 89,810[15], and acetoin[16] from H32 → H32-nox[17] at 75,200[18], both also in fed-batch mode.",
